        "message": "LU-21081 quota: don't let a deferred adjust delay a release\n\nWhen a DQACQ fails with a recoverable error such as -EINPROGRESS,\nthe quota slave queues its next adjust for QSD_WB_INTERVAL later.\nAn immediate adjust request for the same lqe was then ignored\nbecause the lqe was already queued. On ZFS the slave adjusts quota\nonly from the writeback thread after each commit, so the space freed\nby a delete was not released to the master for up to 60 seconds.\nsanity-quota test_63 waits 10 seconds for that release and failed\nwith \"granted N > N after cleanup\".\n\nRequeue a deferred lqe when an immediate adjust is asked for, as is\nalready done for one queued for a per-ID lock cancel.\n\nAdd sanity-quota test_100, which makes one DQACQ fail with\n-EINPROGRESS and checks that the grant is released after the file\nis deleted.\n\nFixes: b2cb6fd1095f (\"LU-1842 quota: add core QSD code\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I65b5f737200113cbb61283613d1ff3f0f68faff0\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
